          "enhanced_information": "Sickle cell disease is primarily caused by a recessive beta-globin mutation, leading to morphological changes in red blood cells and resulting in hemolytic anemia. The abnormality of the RBC membrane causing sickle-shaped RBCs is not the primary pathophysiologic mechanism in sickle cell disease. Relevant evidence supports the genetic basis and morphological changes associated with this condition."
